A||N||8||87ECO5||"Blipping" the throttle on my 3.4 causes the RPMs to drop THEN rise!||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||10-18-2001||09:27 PM||||Have started noticing a disturbing trait of my recently converted 3.4 Fiero.  When sitting still, if I hit the throttle to rev the engine quickly, the RPMs will drop about 200-300 before they begin to rise.<P>Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||10-18-2001||09:38 PM||||Yeah if you’re running the 3.4 injectors than you’re probably running too rich. With my modified 3.4-liter engine and the 3.4 injectors my engine runs too rich and does the same thing.<P>I don't know what to do yet!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||10-18-2001||09:43 PM||||Check your Throttle Position Sensor.<P>My car would do the same thing when the TPS would get stuck.  Mine was a 2.8 however but it still wouldn't hurt to check that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||10-18-2001||09:58 PM||||My TPS checks out fine too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87ECO5||10-18-2001||10:36 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Yeah if you’re running the 3.4 injectors than you’re probably running too rich.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ed Parks used 2.8 injectors for my conversion.<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||10-18-2001||10:37 PM||||Well.. my 3.4 was doing that and was getting worst. Then one day I swaped the MAP sensor from my other car and it stopped. New AC Delco unit solved 98% of it. Still has some hunting but not on bliping. Only when you stop and sometimes. My AutoXray never showed anything noticeable with the bad MAP. Try swaping parts 1st before you buy. The rich due to 3.4 injectors seems possible too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||10-19-2001||09:17 AM||||If nothing else cures it, try playing a little with ignition timing only a degree or 2 at a time.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Turbo88||10-20-2001||01:46 AM||||If you are worried about the possibility of running too rich, try messuring the voltage output from your o2 sensor. Here is a rough break out...<P>Volts - A/F Ratio<BR>0.97V - 12.1:1 Rich<BR>0.88V - 12.7:1<BR>0.78V - 13.2:1 <BR>0.69V - 13.8:1 <BR>0.59V - 14.4:1 <BR>0.49V - 14.9:1 Stoich<BR>0.39V - 15.4:1 <BR>0.30V - 16.0:1 <BR>0.20V - 16.5:1 <BR>0.10V - 17.1:1 Lean<P>The best way to test this is to do it with the engine under load. Fabricate or purchase some long leads and carefully run them into your passenger compartment (those of us who are lazy just run out from under the deck and through the window). Just be careful not to get the wire near the exhaust. Have someone jot down the readings for you at a given RPM and see if you can isolate it. Also check your ecm for codes...<P>Hope this helps<BR>-Bryan||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||10-20-2001||02:31 AM||||Great useful numbers, thanks man!!!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Turbo88:<BR><B>If you are worried about the possibility of running too rich, try messuring the voltage output from your o2 sensor. Here is a rough break out...<P>Volts - A/F Ratio<BR>0.97V - 12.1:1 Rich<BR>0.88V - 12.7:1<BR>0.78V - 13.2:1 <BR>0.69V - 13.8:1 <BR>0.59V - 14.4:1 <BR>0.49V - 14.9:1 Stoich<BR>0.39V - 15.4:1 <BR>0.30V - 16.0:1 <BR>0.20V - 16.5:1 <BR>0.10V - 17.1:1 Lean<P>The best way to test this is to do it with the engine under load. Fabricate or purchase some long leads and carefully run them into your passenger compartment (those of us who are lazy just run out from under the deck and through the window). Just be careful not to get the wire near the exhaust. Have someone jot down the readings for you at a given RPM and see if you can isolate it. Also check your ecm for codes...<P>Hope this helps<BR>-Bryan</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
